  "id": "GCHD",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "The **Global Children's Hazard Database (GCHD)** brings together global, gridded layers of the climate, environmental, geophysical and conflict hazards that children are exposed to: floods, tropical storms, droughts, heatwaves, fire, sand and dust storms, air pollution, malaria, landslides, earthquakes, volcanoes and conflict.\n\nEvery layer is a Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF that can be streamed directly into GIS tools or analysis code. Processing scripts and documentation: https://github.com/unicef/GCHD",
